WEBVTT

00:00:00.012 --> 00:00:04.822
Percentiles help us understand where values fall within a distribution.

00:00:04.822 --> 00:00:11.587
The twenty-fifth percentile is a value below which about twenty-five percent of observations fall.

00:00:11.587 --> 00:00:14.697
The fiftieth percentile is the median.

00:00:14.697 --> 00:00:21.237
The seventy-fifth percentile marks the point below which about seventy-five percent of observations fall.

00:00:21.768 --> 00:00:27.550
These values are useful for describing distributions and for identifying possible outliers.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:34.280
The distance between the seventy-fifth and twenty-fifth percentiles is called the interquartile range,

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.040
often spoken as IQR.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:42.810
Later, you may use IQR rules to flag unusually low or high values.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:48.241
For now, focus on how percentiles divide a distribution into meaningful cutoffs.
